<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Winburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1837 CE – 1848 CE (approx.) · capital Winburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the first Voortrekker states north of the Orange River, a loose Boer community between the Vet and Vaal rivers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-hendrik-potgieter">Andries Hendrik Potgieter</a> obtained land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vet-river">Vet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaal-river">Vaal</a> rivers from the Taung chief Makwana in 1836. After the defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Mzilikazi's Ndebele</a> in 1837, a settlement was laid out whose name, Winburg, is said to recall that victory.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Government was a simple <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad">Volksraad</a> of elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> with a commandant leading the commando. The farmers raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and sheep and dealt with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Sotho</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana</a> neighbours by treaty and raid. From 1843 Winburg was loosely joined with the settlements north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaal-river">Vaal</a> as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/potchefstroom-republic">Potchefstroom-Winburg</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> declared the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/orange-river-sovereignty">Orange River Sovereignty</a> in 1848 and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-boomplaats">Boomplaats</a>. Winburg came under British rule and was later part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/orange-free-state">Orange Free State</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1837 CE – 1848 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.26%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1837 CE – 1848 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Winburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andries Hendrik Potgieter</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Winburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1842&amp;focus=republic-of-winburg" aria-label="Republic of Winburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5387 3222 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Winburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5707 3478L5684 3498"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5684 3498h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5707 3478h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5707 3478h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Winburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1842&amp;focus=republic-of-winburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
